                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="14545828" author="rdblue" created="Fri, 15 May 2015 17:27:30 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Looks like we should probably change that HashMap and make it static. The reason why it wasn&apos;t concurrent is that it is an instance field. But ParquetFileReader keeps a static ParquetMetadataConverter around, assuming that it is thread-safe. At the same time, we should make sure the rest of the class is thread-safe.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14592873" author="alexlevenson" created="Fri, 19 Jun 2015 01:58:24 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;How important is it to cache this state? Simply not cacheing this (and any other instance variables) will make this class thread safe / stateless.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Or, how about using a ThreadLocal cache? Does recomputing this per-thread ruin the performance gain?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14592925" author="alexlevenson" created="Fri, 19 Jun 2015 02:57:27 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Update: the cache was actually never being used as a cache... so I&apos;ve removed the cacheing entirely, and made this class stateless + static&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14592963" author="alexlevenson" created="Fri, 19 Jun 2015 03:41:59 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=yanzt&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;yanzt&quot;&gt;yanzt&lt;/a&gt;, I&apos;ve sent a PR to clean up this class and remove it&apos;s use of a HashMap.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However, I don&apos;t think this was your root issue &amp;#8211; do you know how concurrent access to a HashMap could deadlock? HashMap is not synchronized, so concurrent access probably doesn&apos;t involve locking (for dead lock) and would probably result in undefined return values / behavior or concurrent modification exceptions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Or is there some way it can get into an infinite loop that you know of?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14592964" author="alexlevenson" created="Fri, 19 Jun 2015 03:43:44 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;welp, I&apos;m wrong: &lt;a href=&quot;https://gist.github.com/rednaxelafx/1081908&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://gist.github.com/rednaxelafx/1081908&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
It can cause an infinite loop!&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14594287" author="yanzt" created="Sat, 20 Jun 2015 01:59:52 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the fix. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14594288" author="yanzt" created="Sat, 20 Jun 2015 01:59:59 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the fix. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14600330" author="alexlevenson" created="Wed, 24 Jun 2015 23:02:50 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Issue resolved by pull request 220&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/parquet-mr/pull/220&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/parquet-mr/pull/220&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17857247" author="rok" created="Sun, 23 Jun 2024 03:27:27 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;This issue has been migrated to &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/parquet-java/issues/1812&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;issue #1812&lt;/a&gt; on GitHub. Please see the &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-2502&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;migration documentation&lt;/a&gt; for further details.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
